  "cover_text": "Decreasing biodiversity in an ecosystem can increase the spread of invasive species across an entire ecosystem, and may even result in a decrease in the postinvasive population. Choose an invasive species (please describe at least five examples, but please make sure to cite the specific laws and regulations in your list to make it more interesting and real), then assess the impacts of invasive species on local and global ecosystem processes such as decomposition (how will it affect rates and distribution of decomposers), soil nutrient cycling, plant community composition, or belowground ecosystem services. For example, if your invasive species predicts a disproportionately higher rate of decomposition from organic matter in decomposer communities or soil biota due to to potentially decreased decomposition rates, then use these as a pilot study to explore how certain biological processes and values are over-predicted and under-predicted by invasive species.\nPlease read this paper and upload it below.\nThe title of the paper. The abstract of the paper. The lead and additional all relevant figures.\nYour report that has already been submitted. Provide your copy only without page headers or figures. Measure your joy!\nIntroduction providing a brief statement of why",
